  "question_stem": "A particle moves in a straight line $AB$. The velocity $v \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ of the particle $t \\text{ s}$ after leaving $A$ is given by $v = k(t^2 - 10t + 21)$, where $k$ is a constant. The displacement of the particle from $A$, in the direction towards $B$, is $2.85 \\text{ m}$ when $t = 3$ and is $2.4 \\text{ m}$ when $t = 6$.",
